<title>UK: Major says UK will not join EMU unless convergence.</title>
<headline>Major says UK will not join EMU unless convergence.</headline>
<dateline>LONDON 1997-01-23</dateline>
<text>
<p>Prime Minister John Major said on Thursday that Britain would not join a European single currency unless the countries joining fulfilled the economic convergence criteria.</p>
<p>&quot;If it did proceed without reliable convergence, we would not be part of it,&quot; he told parliament during prime minister's question time.</p>
<p>-- London Newsroom +44-171-542-7768</p>
</text>
